---
// Figure: set only if newer with WATCH, when another writer gets in first.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import './clients.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="clients-watch" title="WATCH: write only if nobody else has" controls="steps"
  caption="A sequence of steps, not a timed simulation. I ran this sequence against Redis 8.10.3 with two connections. The cached entry is a hash with fields version and value. WATCH and HGET share a round trip, as do MULTI, HSET, EXPIRE and EXEC.">
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>Redis caches product:42 at version 8. Writer A, holding version 9 from the database, watches the key and reads the cached version, 8, in one round trip, so it decides to write. Before its write arrives, writer B stores version 10. A's EXEC returns nil and none of its queued commands run. A starts again, reads version 10, which is newer than its own, sends UNWATCH and stops without writing: four round trips, against two when nobody interferes.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { sequenceFigure } from '../shared/sequence.mjs';
  import { watchSpec } from './sequences.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="clients-watch"]').forEach(root => sequenceFigure(root, watchSpec));
</script>
